{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I am El, the Elohim of your father.</b> I am He who said to your father, אַל תֵּרֵד מִצְרָיְמָה (Genesis 26:2); I am He who says to you, <b>do not fear to go down to Egypt</b> — and this is the meaning of <b>for there I will make you a great nation</b>. For had your children remained here, they would have intermarried with the Canaanites and mingled with them. But in Egypt this would not happen, for the Egyptians could not eat bread with the Hebrews, and thus they would become a distinct nation, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said: וַיְהִי שָׁם לְגוֹי (Deuteronomy 26:5) — this teaches that they were distinguished there."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:50.938528446Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}